    "reading": "the pair supremum is a GRID supremum, which can only under-report (the mirror of v6's discrete-ball trap, where a set that was too big over-reported), so the refinement study is part of the measurement.  It is flat to 4e-4 over a 4x refinement in both directions.  The ablation says how much of the constant is the new estimate rather than bookkeeping: with only the pointwise route -- all v6 and v7 had for this quantity -- the same sweep returns a number 240x larger."
  },
